  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">AECF Connect (also referred to as Connect 1.0 in this statement and realted documents) offers services to AECF grantee businesses that are looking to raise capital from impact investors and other related sources. The agreement was signed in December 2012 with a total budget of 16,000,000SEK (all from SIDA), and the activity period ended on 31st March 2019.
AECF Connect focuses on three main strategies to help AECF grantee firms access capital from impact investors and others: 1). targeting grant applicants interested in accessing additional finance; 2). supporting grantee fundraising; and, 3). developing the fundraising market. Connect has provided a range of other services in addition to supporting grantee fundraising.
The Agreement has been amended with non-cost extensions 5 times, since the Agreement was first signed in December 2012. The last and final amendment extended the activity period until 31st of March 2019. 
From inception to date, Connect has set out to achieve the following objectives (aggregated from the original agreement and project proposal together with subsequent amendments). It is worth noting that the Connect 1.0 which was a pilot phase that was suppose to end 30th September 2016, was designed with a very limited logframe, with key performance indicators being gradually added through several amendments of the original agreement.
The main objectives with Connect 1.0, whose performance will be assessed in this completion memo, were the following: 1. Support 14 companies in raising $25m from third party investors and lenders2. Provide fundraising capacity building for 120 companies 3. Connect portfolio companies reach 100,000 households4. Design a follow on phase (Connect 2.0)5. Mobilize funding for Connect 2.06. Carry out an external evaluation of the program</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Creation of a financial brokage function at AECF for more leverage of private financing of agribusinesses within the AECF portfolio.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Skapa en finansiell enhet som ska underl&#xe4;tta &#xf6;kad finansering till jordbruksrelaterade f&#xf6;retag i Afrika inom AECF portf&#xf6;ljen.</narrative>
  </description>
